SUMMARY: Killer B Cinema Presents: Messiah of Evil!
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, November 6th\, join us for the obscure horror fil
 m Messiah of Evil!\n\nAdvanced tickets are $5 (plus Eventbrite service fe
 e)\; tickets at the door are $8 (Space is limited\, and tickets sell out 
 fast)!\n\nTickets: www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002890558577?aff=oddtdtcreator ht
 tps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002890558577?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\nTrailer: you
 tu.be/lCrGJFvo6Ec?si=tCYh2YGaKd6hklOO https://youtu.be/lCrGJFvo6Ec?si=tCY
 h2YGaKd6hklOO\n\nDoors open at 7:30 pm\, and the movie begins at 8:00.\n\
 n*NO outside food or drinks\; please buy food and drinks from the venue.\
 n\n*All films have closed captioning.\n\nMovie info:\n\nIt might be Novem
 ber\, but it’s still spooky season for us!\n\nMessiah of Evil (1973) is a
  surreal\, slow-burn horror film about a young woman who travels to the e
 erie seaside town of Point Dume\, California\, searching for her missing 
 artist father. She finds his abandoned home and a disturbing diary warnin
 g of strange changes overtaking the town. As she investigates\, she encou
 nters increasingly bizarre residents\, ritualistic behavior\, and a growi
 ng sense that something ancient and horrifying is approaching. The film b
 lends occult horror\, zombies\, and dreamlike imagery into an unsettling 
 story of isolation and creeping doom.\n\nThis is the perfect movie to hel
 p us creep into the darker months.\n\nInfo about See-Scape:\n\nOur movies
  will be shown on the second floor! There are two bars available in See-S
 cape. The bar on the second floor is open during our event and is cash-on
 ly. Debit/Credit purchases are available on the main floor.\n\nSee-Scape 
 also has an amazing menu. To learn more about See-Scape\, please click he
 re! www.seescapeto.com/ https://www.seescapeto.com/\n\nSee-Scape is locat
 ed at 347 Keele Street (the closest intersection is Keele/Dundas) and is 
 easily accessible via TTC. (from Keele Station or Dundas West Station)\n\
 nParking: There is a Green P parking lot beside See-Scape and a few other
  paid parking lots nearby.\n\nEach month\, join Lizzie Violet & Zoltan Du
  Lac for killer B-moves from the 1930s to the present!\n\nPlease like our
  Facebook page and Instagram @killerbcinema so you don’t miss an invite.\
 n\nThank you to See-Scape and their staff! They make our monthly event ex
 tra unforgettable!\n\nWe hope to see you at See-Scape.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Film,See-Scape
