SUMMARY:UNHack
DTSTART:20261107T050000Z
DTEND:20261109T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20261014T154700Z
UID:MEC-683768cf9ad8eecfd2e847498002cd29@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261107T050000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 0/Square.png
CATEGORIES:Faculties
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261014
DESCRIPTION:UNHack 2026 is a two-day hackathon hosted by YSpace and the La
 ssonde School of Engineering at York University\, bringing together engine
 ering students to tackle real-world challenges inspired by the United Nati
 ons Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\nParticipation does not need a s
 tartup idea\, previous hackathon experience\, or advanced technical skills
 . Through the programming you’ll be guided through a structured process 
 that takes you from problem → idea → prototype → pitch\, with suppor
 t from mentors\, facilitators\, and technical experts along the way.\nKEY 
 DETAILS\n📅 When\n\nSaturday\, November 7 – Sunday\, November 8\, 2026
 \n\n📍 Where\n\nBergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence\, York Univer
 sity\n\n👥 Who Can Participate\nUNHack is open to ANY undergraduate stud
 ent at York University. You can register:\n\nIndividually – we’ll help
  match you with a team\nWith a pre-formed team of 3–5 students\n\n💡 W
 hat You’ll Do\nOver two days\, you’ll:\n1. Identify a problem\nExplore
  selected UN Sustainable Development Goal challenge tracks and define a fo
 cused How Might We (HMW) problem statement.\n2. Develop your solution\nGen
 erate ideas\, understand your users\, evaluate existing alternatives\, and
  select a concept to pursue.\n3. Build a prototype\nTurn your idea into an
  achievable prototype or MVP with dedicated build time\, workshops\, techn
 ical support\, and mentor office hours.\n4. Pitch your solution\nDevelop a
 nd practice your pitch before presenting your solution to judges. Top team
 s will advance to the final round and pitch on the main stage.\n🏆 PRIZE
 S & OPPORTUNITIES\n\nCash prizes for 1st\, 2nd\, and 3rd place teams\nMent
 orship from industry professionals and technical experts\nHands-on experie
 nce with design thinking\, prototyping\, and pitching\nExperience Ventures
 : The first 60 eligible domestic students may receive. $325 upon successfu
 l completion of the hackathon and associated program requirements. Funding
  is first-come\, first-served and subject to eligibility.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014
LOCATION:Room 313\, Bergeron Centre\, YorkU Keele Campus
ORGANIZER;CN=YSpace:MAILTO:yspace@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/unhack/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
