SUMMARY:Model Mondays - Spotlight on NVIDIA models
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nNVIDIA models give developers optio
 ns for building and deploying AI workloads that require strong reasoning\,
  generation\, and accelerated inference across a range of application scen
 arios.\n\nJoin us as we explore NVIDIA models in Microsoft Foundry and see
  how they can be evaluated and used to build effective AI agents.\n---\n\n
 * Explore the Resources https://github.com/microsoft/model-mondays\n* Read
  the Newsletter https://aka.ms/model-mondays/newsletter\n* Continue the co
 nversation on the Discord https://aka.ms/model-mondays/discord\n\n[event I
 D:27577]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3164
 23217/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260904T222612Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T222612Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4809214407827f8aa92cda"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Nature TO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T150000
UID:6a4809214407827f8aa92cda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Humber Summit Library and its neighbourhood is home to a v
 ariety of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nto explor
 e the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize 
 different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological import
 ance.\nFree program. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/car
 egiver. Registration is required.\nPresented as part of TPL’s environmen
 tal program series\, Our Fragile Planet. The series is generously supporte
 d by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nThe tour\nwill be
  guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\,
  unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly fo
 r this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, c
 omfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of
  severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative
  date.
LOCATION:Humber Summit
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4809214407827f8aa92cda
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
