BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a33b6c71003e5de7bb"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Run Your One-Person Business with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T200000
UID:6a9b51a33b6c71003e5de7bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When you're the whole company\, the admin never ends: emails\,
  scheduling\, proposals\, follow-ups. What if you could design a system to
  handle the busywork?\nIn this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\n
 Ryan Kelln\n\, you'll learn to design an administrative system for a one-p
 erson business with AI as your assistant: intake pipelines\, email draftin
 g\, client communication\, and scheduling. Learn to map work into four pil
 es: what's rules-based\, what AI drafts\, what needs your judgment\, and w
 hat should never be automated. You'll build reusable templates and leave w
 ith a clearer plan for how AI could help your business.\nPrerequisites: M
 ouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No codin
 g experience required.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\
 , 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minute
 s of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be 
 filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached. If 
 you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your 
 own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program incl
 udes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptop
 s.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticip
 ants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout session
 s\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review 
 the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClau
 de Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\n
 Learn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn 
 more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
 d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\,
  delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416
 -397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a33b6c71003e5de7bb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
