CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Progra
 ms),Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Gradu
 ate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Gr
 aduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate 
 Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate P
 rogram in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp\; Media Studies,Gradua
 te Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Cult
 ure,Graduate Program in Conference Interpreting,Graduate Program in Critic
 al Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design
 ,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media
 ,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp\; Emergency Management,Graduate Program
  in Earth &amp\; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Prog
 ram in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp\; Communi
 ty Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp\; Computer S
 cience,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studi
 es,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,G
 raduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gend
 er, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Pr
 ogram in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in Hist
 ory,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Hum
 anities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp\; Technology,Graduate
  Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and 
 Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &am
 p\; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate P
 rogram in Mathematics &amp\; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Eng
 ineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Pr
 ogram in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp\; Astronomy,Graduate 
 Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Progr
 am in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &a
 mp\; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp\; Political Though
 t,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,
 Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Grad
 uate Program in Theatre,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp\; Performa
 nce Studies,Graduate Program in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Vi
 sual Art
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20251114
DESCRIPTION:\nThe Certificate in Personal Wellness is a supportive and enr
 iching experience designed to nurture personal well-being and promote bala
 nce in everyday life. Participants will explore practical\, evidence-infor
 med strategies for reducing stress\, understanding and managing negative t
 hought patterns\, and building emotional resilience. Drawing from the fiel
 d of positive psychology\, the series introduces empowering practices such
  as mindfulness\, gratitude\, and self-compassion—skills that encourage 
 greater self-awareness\, inner calm\, and a more compassionate relationshi
 p with oneself. Aspects of Cognitive Behavioural Therapy and Dialetical Be
 haviour Therapy will be included.\n\n\n\nDates: October 20\, 27\, Novembe
 r 3\, 10 & 17​\n\n\n\n\nTime: 10:30 A.M. – 12:00 P.M. (ET)\nOpen to: G
 raduate Students\n\n\n\n\nRegistration: The Certificate in Personal Wellne
 ss (Fall 2026) – Fill out form ( https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/C62V7mF
 caG )\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817
LOCATION:Zoom Session
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/certificate-in-personal-wellness/
