SEQUENCE:7
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 11/sen.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261102
DESCRIPTION:Sensorium: Centre for Digital Arts and Technology ( https://am
 pd.yorku.ca/sensorium/ ) and the School of the Arts\, Media\, Performance 
 & Design at York University are pleased to the present\, Shimmering Method
 s: Research Creation Across Art\, Science\, and Emerging Technologies\, a 
 new interdisciplinary speaker series developed and co-presented with the O
 ffice of the Associate Dean Research\, School of the Arts\, Media\, Perfor
 mance\, and Design\, and the Creative Collectivities Project (funded by Co
 nnected Minds ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/connected-minds/ )).\nThe fi
 rst Lunch & Learn features a talk by Professor Maria Chatzichristodoulou
 \, Principal Investigator of The Abundance Project\, a major research st
 udy exploring impacts of arts and social prescribing on communities in the
  UK. A renowned scholar of Performance and Digital transformation\, Chatzi
 christodoulou will present the project’s journey and consider the appl
 icability of their key findings and interventions to contexts beyond Londo
 n and the UK.\nDate: November 10\, 2026\nTime: 12:00 – 1:30 p.m.\nLocati
 on: Sensorium Loft\, Room M333\, 4th floor\, Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts
  (CFA)\, York University\nFree. RSVP  Here ( https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfuJMD_Fu2zERtb8nEgzYVeTC9idYTrn0KMfZ4oHRcx0Mw8og/viewform )
 .\nLunch will be provided in limited amounts to those who RSVP in advance 
 for the session.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105
LOCATION:Sensorium Loft\, 4th Floor of Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts @ 86 
 Fine Arts Rd
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/shimmering-methods-research-creation-ac
 ross-art-science-and-emerging-technologies/
