SUMMARY:The Gravity Grand Prix: Race Day Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T190000
UID:6ad67f0ea85a2c003380a315@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The wait is over—it’s time to race! After a week of design
 ing\, building\, and testing\, teams will put their 3D-printed gravity-pow
 ered race cars to the ultimate test. Compete against other teams to see wh
 ose car can conquer the downhill track the fastest and take home the title
  of Gravity Grand Prix Champion!\n🏁\nThe Competition\nThe Race:\nTeams 
 will race their completed 3D-printed cars on the downhill track to determi
 ne the fastest design.\nThe Goal:\nPut your engineering skills to the test
  and see how your design performs in the ultimate speed challenge.\nWho Ca
 n Participate:\nThis competition is exclusively for teams who participated
  in the first part of the Gravity Grand Prix: the design and prototyping c
 hallenge.\n📅\nRace Day: November 11\nBring your car\, bring your compet
 itive spirit\, and get ready to race! Family and friends are welcome to co
 me watch the final showdown as teams compete for the Gravity Grand Prix ti
 tle.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Inside the DIH
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad67f0ea85a2c003380a315
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
