DESCRIPTION:York International (YI) is accepting proposals for faculty-led
  study abroad courses and programs for 2027/28 and 2028/29.\nYI offers man
 y supports to faculty leads and instructors including international partne
 rship support\, program and budget planning and vendor-service provider co
 ordination\, student recruitment and promotions\, logistical arrangements\
 , student funding\, safety abroad training and travel risk management. Stu
 dents may also be eligible for York International Mobility Award (YIMA) up
 on completion of safety abroad training and procedures.\nWe have funding a
 vailable to support students studying abroad in the following destinations
 \, and we encourage faculty members to consider developing faculty-led stu
 dy abroad courses in these locations:\n\nChina (Canada Learning Initiative
  in China\, CLIC funding)\nGermany (3 Endowed Awards)\n\nWe also have coll
 eagues at the University of Leeds (UK) who can provide the support and inf
 rastructure including accommodation and excursions for developing faculty-
 led study abroad courses in Leeds\, England.\nInterested faculty members a
 re strongly encouraged to attend a Faculty-led Study Abroad Course Info Se
 ssion on Wednesday\, Nov. 11 from 2 t0 3 p.m. Please register here.\nThos
 e interested in leading a study abroad course/program can register their i
 nterest through Faculty-Led Study Abroad Proposal Form on or before Nov. 3
 0\, for help planning and designing the program. Note that all application
 s received will be discussed with relevant colleagues in the faculty for a
 pproval by the academic unit.\nFor any questions\, please feel free to rea
 ch out to us at yuabroad@yorku.ca ( mailto:yuabroad@yorku.ca ).\n
