BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/unsettling-the-public-record-decolonial-research-methods-for-troubling-times/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Unsettling the Public Record: Decolonial Research Methods for Trou
 bling Times
DTSTART:20261112T170000Z
DTEND:20261112T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T212800Z
UID:MEC-1297bcaf6f829c2afe9cae03f1975683@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261112T170000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 0/Alexandra-workshop.png
CATEGORIES:Networking Opportunities (CCC),Workshops &amp\; Webinars (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261023
DESCRIPTION:\nAs censorship and retaliation become growing concerns\, turn
 ing to public records and events as sources of ethnographic data raises im
 portant ethical questions. Guided by Black feminist critiques of archival 
 violence\, Alexandra will examine how the very idea of what is considered 
 “public” can reproduce harm and shape the people and communities repre
 sented within public records.\nThe session will explore the situated ethic
 al obligations that emerge when conducting ethnographic research in and th
 rough publics\, and consider how research practices can not only unsettle 
 the public record\, but contribute to building more just worlds in troubli
 ng times.\nParticipants are welcome to attend all three sessions. Zoom det
 ails will be shared with registered participants ahead of each workshop.\n
 \nREGISTER HERE\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023
ORGANIZER;CN="Connected Minds":MAILTO:connectedmindsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/unsettling-the-public-record-decolonial
 -research-methods-for-troubling-times/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
