SUMMARY:Food Justice in Toronto: Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6ac3e146a85a2c00337d59a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Food is about more than what's for dinner.\nJoin an expert-led
  discussion on the right to food and how we can increase access to food in
  our community. We will learn about Toronto's food system and strategize t
 o address food insecurity and inequity. The panel will conclude with a gro
 up reflection and discussion on how we engage with our local food systems.
 \nPanelists include:\nShath Ramesh\n(she/they) is a community organizer an
 d the Urban Agriculture Coordinator at Malvern Family Resource Centre\, wh
 ere they manage the Malvern Urban Farmers' Market. They hold a Masters in 
 sustainability studies from Trent University and are passionate about food
  justice\, climate action and advocacy.\nJade Guthrie\n(she/her) is a que
 er\, mixed-race educator\, facilitator\, and community organizer. As the M
 anager of Community Learning and Engagement at FoodShare Toronto\, jade is
  committed to social change work rooted in justice\, liberation\, and joy 
 and approaches this work with tenderness\, curiosity\, and reciprocity. Be
 yond 9-5\, jade is an organizer with Justicia for Migrant Workers\, a boar
 d member at Food Secure Canada\, and sits on the City of Toronto’s Black
  Food Sovereignty Action Plan Advisory Circle.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac3e146a85a2c00337d59a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
