SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T160000
UID:6a0622accaf93436005beec8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nFri
 day\, October 16\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a week fo
 r 8 weeks\, October 23 to December 11\n. Registration closes after week 3\
 , or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshm
 ents are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availabl
 e at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis 
 Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible f
 or the protection of \npersonal information collected through the program 
 registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 3rd floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0622accaf93436005beec8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc1b8fe8cf1c005cafeaac"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) for Healthy Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T160000
UID:6abc1b8fe8cf1c005cafeaac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being
 —whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or s
 imply wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRA
 P for Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is e
 xpertly designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the 
 principles of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging 
 challenges\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experien
 ce with WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skills
 .\nParticipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program c
 ompletion\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. Fi
 nd more WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every Fr
 iday\, once a week for 3 weeks\, November 13\, November 20\, November 27.)
  Week 1 will be 3 hours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  W
 RAP\; Weeks 2 and 3 will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provide
 d\n.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredien
 t lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborat
