SUMMARY:Aki no Tabi | 秋の旅
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T190000
UID:1e43949a1b1cd702dee939d13411dc35@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Aki no Tabi — Autumn at the JCCC This fall\, join us at the 
 JCCC for a new seasonal experience celebrating Japanese and Japanese Canad
 ian culture through creativity\, connection\, and hands-on activities. Ins
 pired by the nostalgic charm of Japan and the cozy feeling of autumn trans
 itioning into winter\, Aki no Tabi is a place to slow down\, create\, conn
 ect\, and enjoy the season together. Come experience the warmth and nostal
 gia of autumn at the JCCC. 🍂 Keep an eye on this space for more detaile
 d information in the coming weeks! Schedule Ongoing Activities (1pm-7pm) P
 aradise Exhibition Autumn Market (Marketplace Vendors) Artisans' Town (Han
 ds-on Activity Area) Feast Alley (JCCC Food & Food Vendors) Story Alley (J
 CCC Library & Book Sale) 1:00 pm - 7:00 pm Time Specific Events Live Music
  by Spare Bedroom Main Entrance 2:30 pm - 4:00 pm A.S.M. Kobayashi Artist 
 Talk Heritage Court 3:00 pm - 4:00 pm Live Music by Spare Bedroom Main Ent
 rance 5:00 pm - 6:30 pm Workshops (Tickets on Sale!) Journaling & Paper Cr
 aft - Crafting Our Narratives with Erica H. Isomura and Nico Koyanagi Saku
 ra Room 1:30 pm - 4:00 pm Ceramics - Autumn Leaves Mamezara with Secret Te
 atime Heritage Lounge 1:30 pm - 3:00 pm Crochet - Make Your Own Amigurumi 
 with So Craftful MNHC Museum 1:30 pm - 3:30 pm Wagashi Making - Enjoy Daif
 uku with Atelier Wa Wynford Room 2:00 pm - 3:30 pm Ceramics - Autumn Leave
 s Mamezara with Secret Teatime Heritage Lounge 4:00 pm - 5:30 pm Crochet -
  Make Your Own Amigurumi with So Craftful MNHC Museum 4:00 pm - 6:00 pm Wa
 gashi Making - Enjoy Daifuku with Atelier Wa Wynford Room 4:30 pm - 6:00 p
 m Autumn Market Marketplace Vendors Feast Alley JCCC Food & Food Vendors A
 rtisans' Town Hands-on Activity Vendors Create a cute fruit parfait photo 
 and memo holder with air-dry clay. A fun 30-minute activity for all ages. 
 Fee: $10 Make a mini wreath or bouquet necklace. Add lava stones for essen
 tial oils or dried flowers for a personal touch. Fee: $20 Explore ceramic 
 fracture patterns and transfer your favorite design onto a pendant to crea
 te a unique kintsugi keepsake. Fee: $30 (Chain sold separately) A beautifu
 l mix of hand-selected succulents\, each featuring unique shapes\, texture
 s\, and colours. A lovely\, low-maintenance addition to any home or a thou
 ghtful gift for someone special. Fee: $19.99 Explore tarot for guidance an
 d inspiration or try your luck with a traditional Japanese omikuji fortune
  slip. Tarot Readings: $10-$58 Omikuji: $2 Discover 19th-century rug hooki
 ng and quilting with costumed interpreters\, then create your own quilt sq
 uare to take home. Fee: By donation Design a button badge featuring histor
 ic photos from the JCCC Archives. Meet our team and discover how we preser
 ve Japanese Canadian heritage. Fee: By donation Create your own keychain o
 r water bottle holder using paracord. Choose from a variety of colours\, p
 atterns\, and charms to make it your own. Fee: $12-15 A.S.M. Kobayashi Art
 ist Talk Join award-winning interdisciplinary artist A.S.M. Kobayashi for 
 an engaging talk exploring her creative practice through found recordings\
 , everyday objects\, performance\, and storytelling. Discover her 20-year 
 artistic journey\, including her acclaimed performance Say Something Bunny
 !\, and her latest work\, Electric Neon Clock\, which transforms her famil
 y's WWII internment records into an immersive installation combining archi
 val materials\, video\, sound\, and performance. A.S.M. Kobayashi Based in
  Toronto and NYC\, A.S.M. Kobayashi is an internationally recognized artis
 t working across performance\, video\, installation\, and illustration. Sh
 e is a Creative Capital Awardee and a fellow of Yaddo and MacDowell. Her s
 olo exhibition\, Electric Neon Clock\, is on view at the Art Gallery of Mi
 ssissauga until October 25\, with live performances from October 21–24.\
 n\nCategories: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/11/aki-no-tabi
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
