 dent Life,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,W
 ell-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a one-hour\, student-designed workshop that explor
 es how gambling and sports betting show up in campus life. Created in coll
 aboration with the Responsible Gambling Council (RGC)\, the session uses i
 nteractive activities and real examples to help you stay informed and in c
 ontrol.\nYou’ll learn to:\n\nSpot early signs of gambling-related harm\n
 Practice strategies to support yourself and friends\nDiscover on-campus an
 d provincial supports\n\nParticipants who attend the full session will rec
 eive a $5 gift card by email after the workshop. As gift cards are tied to
  full-session participation\, they are not available for those who attend 
 only part of the session. Space is limited and registration is first-come\
 , first-served. If the session is full and you’d like to be added to the
  waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca ). We
 ’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re registered but ca
 n no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as possible so we can offe
 r your spot to another student.\nRegister for Books Before Bets\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918
LOCATION:Register for Zoom Link
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
