X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | Navigating Financial Challenges & Building Resili
 ence
DTSTART:20261117T223000Z
DTEND:20261118T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261028T190800Z
UID:MEC-57cb680116490a4c6c0bb57a8fa476f1@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261117T223000Z
SEQUENCE:11
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 2/Mentor-Circles.png
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261028
DESCRIPTION:Date: Tuesday Nov. 17\nTime: 5:30 – 7 p.m.\nLocation: 280N Y
 ork Lanes\, York University\nMentor Circles is collaborating with Black Ex
 cellence at York University (BE YU) for a financial literacy workshop.\nDu
 ring this session\, you will learn:\n\nStrategies for handling debt\, unex
 pected expenses\, and limited income\nLeveraging campus\, community\, and 
 financial institution resources\nBuilding habits that strengthen financial
  resilience and confidence\n\nAlumni speaker: Tinotenda Mutsvangwa (BA ’
 20\, MSTM ’21)\, Financial Advisor at CIBC\n\nTinotenda is a devoted CIB
 C Imperial Service Financial Advisor\, holding both the (CSC) and (CPH) ce
 rtifications. With a bachelor’s degree in Political Science and a master
 ’s in Business Management from Schulich School of Business\, Tino combin
 es academic excellence with practical expertise to deliver exceptional fin
 ancial solutions. Tino received was recently selected as one of York Unive
 rsity’s Top 30 Under 30 Alumni for 2025.\n \n \n \n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028
LOCATION:280N York Lanes @ 4700 Keele St\, North York\, ON M3J 1P3\, Canad
 a
ORGANIZER;CN="Office of Alumni Engagement":MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-navigating-financial-cha
 llenges-building-resilience/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/navigating-financial-challenges-building-resilience-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Navigating Financial Challenges & Building Resilience
DTSTART:20261117T223000Z
DTEND:20261118T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T211700Z
UID:MEC-90e67987539164c4f62dd88d4558b1d6@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261117T223000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Financial Literacy Month
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261019
DESCRIPTION:Mentor Circles: Navigating Financial Challenges & Building Res
 ilience is a collaboration with the Black Excellence at York University (B
 E YU) program. This is an engaging session designed to equip students with
  practical strategies to navigate financial challenges\, build financial c
 onfidence\, and strengthen their financial resilience. Through real-world 
 insights and actionable advice\, students will explore strategies for mana
 ging debt\, preparing for unexpected expenses\, and making the most of lim
 ited income. The session will also highlight campus\, community\, and fina
 ncial institution resources that can support students’ financial well-be
 ing\, while emphasizing the importance of developing healthy financial hab
 its\, making informed financial decisions\, and building a strong foundati
 on for long-term financial stability. Join us for an insightful conversati
 on with Tinotenda Mutsvangwa (BA ’20\, MSTM ’21)\, Financial Advisor a
 t CIBC\, as he shares his knowledge and professional experience to help st
 udents navigate financial uncertainty\, overcome common financial challeng
 es\, and develop the confidence and skills needed to make informed financi
 al choices. \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019
LOCATION:280N York Lanes
ORGANIZER;CN="Black Excellence at York University":MAILTO:beyu@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/navigating-financial-challenges-buildin
 g-resilience-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
