SUMMARY: Cocktails for a Cause Fundraiser
DESCRIPTION:The WoodGreen Foundation’s Young Leaders Council (YLC) https:
 //www.woodgreen.org/about-the-foundation will host its annual Cocktails f
 or a Cause fundraiser on November 17\, 2026\, at the Art Gallery of Ontar
 io (AGO)\, bringing together Toronto’s young professionals and community 
 leaders for an evening dedicated to raising awareness and support of Wood
 Green’s new Youth Wellness Centre.\n\nWoodGreen Foundation’s YLC brings t
 ogether emerging philanthropists and community-minded professionals commi
 tted to addressing some of Toronto’s most pressing social challenges. Thr
 ough fundraising\, community engagement and education\, YLC members mobil
 ize their networks to advance WoodGreen’s mandate and create meaningful l
 ocal impact.\n\nGuests will enjoy an engaging evening connecting with Tor
 onto’s young professionals\, community leaders and changemakers over cock
 tails and a curated culinary experience. The event will feature a firesid
 e chat with distinguished leaders from the world of sports\, including 20
 26 Winter Olympics bronze medallist and five-time Canadian national champ
 ion ice dancer Piper Gilles https://olympic.ca/team-canada/piper-gilles/ 
 \, and Lisa Ferkul https://www.linkedin.com/in/lisaferkul/ \, Chief Reven
 ue Officer of the Toronto Tempo https://tempo.wnba.com/ .\n\nGuests will 
 also receive exclusive access to an exhibit at the AGO\, alongside a sile
 nt auction and a lucky draw featuring prizes donated by local businesses 
 - all in support of WoodGreen’s one-stop social services hub for youth.\n
 \nWoodGreen’s Youth Wellness Centre https://www.woodgreen.org/programs/yo
 uth-wellness-centre provides young people aged 12–29 a full range of free
  services\, including settlement support\, housing\, employment\, educati
 on\, financial assistance and cultural programming. The Centre also offer
 s free wellness workshops and skill-building opportunities to help young 
 people access resources and build skills for the future.\n\n“Cocktails fo
 r a Cause is an opportunity for Toronto’s next generation of leaders to t
 urn their passion for community into meaningful action\,” said Olivia Cla
 rk https://www.linkedin.com/in/olivia-clark-a22193125/ \, Chair of WoodGr
 een’s YLC. “We look forward to bringing people together at the iconic AGO
  to support the essential wrap-around services WoodGreen offers young peo
 ple as they navigate important stages of their lives.”\n\nEvent Details:\
 n\n● Date: Tuesday\, November 17\, 2026\n\n● Time: 6:00-9:00 p.m. ET\n\n●
  Location: Art Gallery of Ontario\, Walker Court\, 317 Dundas Street West
 \, Toronto\, ON M5T 1G4\n\n● Tickets: https://trellis.org/ylcscocktailsfo
 racause https://trellis.org/ylcscocktailsforacause
CATEGORIES:In-Conversation,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Art-Gallery-of-Ontario
