X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T153000
UID:6ad6202febad2200454657c0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn how to maintain your online privac
 y and how to secure your online accounts and devices? If so\, this is the 
 class for you. Come and join us in this introductory session that is fille
 d with hands-on activities and discussion.\nIn this program\, you will:\nL
 earn how to maintain your online privacy through good habits and the secur
 ity of your accounts and devices.\nDevelop a strong password\, and review 
 the best methods for storing your passwords.\nLearn about various online t
 hreats: malware\, phishing\, hacking\, etc.\nGain an understanding of the 
 limitations of these tools and habits.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad6202febad2200454657c0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad24ff5ebad22004545d31e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T153000
UID:6ad24ff5ebad22004545d31e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a 6-week course designed to build y
 our confidence by introducing new skills slowly in a small\, supportive co
 mmunity. At the end of the course\, you may not know everything about the 
 internet\, but you will have a solid foundation of new skills and the conf
 idence to continue learning.\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as th
 e mouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services 
 and entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and frien
 ds\nInternet safety\, security and privacy\nWeek 1:\nUse the Mouse\nWeek 2
 :\nUse the Keyboard\nWeek 3:\nUse Windows\nWeek 4:\nUse the Internet\nWeek
  5:\nUse Google Search & Maps\nWeek 6:\nUse Email (Gmail)\nThe class is li
 mited to\n8\nparticipants. Registration is required\, please register on t
 he TPL website. If you need any assistance with registering\, please visit
  us in-branch\, or call us at 416-393-7674. When registering\, you will be
