SUMMARY:Ask a Nurse Drop-by Tabling Session
DTSTART:20261118T180000Z
DTEND:20261118T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T192800Z
UID:MEC-21c6d7a1fc87615fa44ae7657a773566@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261118T180000Z
SEQUENCE:12
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Advising,Ask a Nurse,H
 ealth Education &amp\; Promotion,Markham Campus,Student Counselling, Healt
 h &amp\; Well-being,Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:Consult a healthcare professional\nStudents juggle a lot\, fro
 m academics and work to family and friends. It can be hard to prioritize y
 our own health and well-being at the same time.\nAsk a Nurse is a confide
 ntial service for York students. Speak to Public Health Nurses from Studen
 t Counselling\, Health & Well-being about your health-related questions\, 
 without an appointment. There is a lot of health-related information onlin
 e and it can be difficult to tell what’s reliable. Our goal is to answer
  your questions\, find solutions and connect you to the most helpful resou
 rces. Come see us in-person or get in touch online ( https://students.yor
 ku.ca/health/ask-a-nurse )!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918
LOCATION:Markham Campus 1st Floor Atrium
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ask-a-nurse-drop-by-tabling-session-10-
 687-808-772-258-553/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-5-financial-literacy-understanding-your-student-financial-responsibility/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 5 | Financial literacy: Unders
 tanding your student financial responsibility
DTSTART:20261118T180000Z
DTEND:20261118T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T190600Z
UID:MEC-e265b71426b39bb25ccf6eca0a578a03@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261118T180000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Glendon,Markham Campus
 ,Markham Student Accessibility Services,Student Leaders at Markham (SLAM),
 Student Life
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session is open to students from York’s Markham and Gle
 ndon campuses.\nTuition\, textbooks\, bus fares\, lunch\, getting a coffee
  or energy drink to get through your 2nd lecture of the day… expenses ad
 d up quickly when you’re in university.\nIn this week’s session of YU 
 & Balance\, participants will:\n\nGet a realistic overview of their financ
 ial responsibilities\nLearn how to save money on campus\, build balanced b
 udgets and understand the differences between types of student debt.\nStud
 ents will also get a chance to ask Peer Health Educators for advice\, tips
  and strategize on how to be more money conscious.\n\nThis session is part
  of a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, particip
 ants will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must
  attend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, 
 we’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards 
 will be emailed after the session to the same email address used to regist
 er and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered o
 n a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d li
 ke to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hs
 tacey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’
