X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaedabbca248a002916fe35"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Tutankhamun: The Sensational Discovery - Part 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T193000
UID:6aaedabbca248a002916fe35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year marks an important anniversary in the history of Egy
 ptology. On November 4th\, 2026\, it will be 104 years since Howard Carter
  and Lord Carnarvon discovered the intact tomb of King Tutankhamun in 1922
  - a discovery that continues to capture the public imagination.\nNearly a
  year after the complete collection went on display at the Grand Egyptian 
 Museum in Cairo on November 1\, 2025\, Egyptologist Sherine ElSebaie will 
 take audiences back to the time of its discovery. Following the footsteps 
 of the excavators\, she will conclude the story of the discovery and explo
 re the remarkable objects found in the burial chamber and the treasury dur
 ing the excavation of 1923.\nRegistration is encouraged but not required.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1 (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaedabbca248a002916fe35
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad918878a335b6ae5c9e405"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: Active Listening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T190000
UID:6ad918878a335b6ae5c9e405@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\n6\n0-minute\nsessi
 on.\nDemocracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by e
 xploring the skills that help people participate in civic life\, build con
 nection\, and work better together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise ou
 r\nActive Listening\nMuscle:\nIn a democracy\, everyone has the right to s
 peak. Being heard requires that someone listens. When you listen openly an
 d with curiosity\, you create understanding and trust.\nRegistration Recom
 mended. Drop-ins welcome.\nAdults only.\nThis program is offered in partne
 rship with Democracy Fitness Global and MASS LBP.\nGenerously supported by
  McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad918878a335b6ae5c9e405
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
