X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_arts_and_culture
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Arts & Culture
UID:event_316866080@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055714Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T213000
SUMMARY:Koerner Hall:  Naghash Ensemble\, Karen Ouzounian\, and the Amadeu
 s Choir
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n**A magical evening of Armenian music 
 direct from Yerevan\, and the Canadian premiere of *Dear Mountains*\,** a 
 recent work for chorus\, solo cello\, oud\, and percussion\, co-composed b
 y the RCM alumna and Silk Road Ensemble member Karen Ouzounian and Lembit 
 Beecher.\n\nPlease **use our 15% off promo code** for this concert. Detail
 s/Ticket link is below. (Excellent pricing and seats on this concert)\n\n*
 *The Naghash Ensemble** combines the earthy spirituality of Armenian folk 
 songs\, new classical music\, and contemporary post-minimalism with the en
 ergy of rock and jazz. Three brilliant female vocalists and some of Armeni
 a’s finest instrumentalists on duduk\, oud\, dhol\, and piano play capti
 vating new music based on sacred texts by the medieval Armenian mystic poe
 t and priest Mkrtich Naghash.\n\nWritten by Armenian-American composer Joh
 n Hodian\, The Naghash Ensemble’s *Songs of Exile* is a profound meditat
 ion on man's relationship to God from the perspective of a monk forced to 
 live in exile for many years. Part folk music\, part classical\, and profo
 undly moving.\n\nSought after for her “radiant” (*The New York Times*)
  performances full of “tremendous heart\, bringing joy and a captivating
  sound to the stage” (*The Strad*)\, Karen Ouzounian is a Grammy Award n
 ominated cellist and composer who creates music from a deeply personal pla
 ce. An omnivorous musical spirit who “powerfully shatters pigeonholes wi
 th her artistic partners” (*Ravinia Magazine*)\, she has premiered numer
 ous works and collaborated with some of the most singular musicians of our
  time\, including Yo-Yo Ma\, Rhiannon Giddens\, and Augustin Hadelich. She
  will present *Dear Mountains*\, a major work composed by her and Lembit B
 eecher in 2024 that juxtaposes stories told and retold in Ouzounian’s fa
 mily with scenes of music-making across the Armenian diaspora over the las
 t 100 years\, as seen through archival recordings and writings. *Dear Moun
 tains* features Ouzounian on cello\, Ara Dinkjian on oud\, Philip Mayer on
  percussion\, **and the Amadeus Choir led by Kathleen Allan.**\nLed by Art
 istic Director Kathleen Allan\, the Amadeus Choir champions the best of ch
 oral music and premieres works of Canadian and international composers thr
 ough a self-produced Toronto concert series\, guest performances\, and spe
 cial events. The Choir regularly commissions work from high-profile and em
 erging Canadian composers and recently established the Choral Creation Lab
 \, a residency for composers and poets to co-create original works.\n\n**T
 icket link here-**-(and videos of the artists)\n\nhttps://www.rcmusic.com/
 concert/naghash-ensemble-karen-ouzounian-quartet-and-the-amadeus-choir-448
 401\n\n**Use promo code** ISCULTURE15 (for 15% off pricing)\n\nPlay around
  with the seating chart. I am in LOGE 11 (Lower Balcony)\n\n\\*\\*\\*Pleas
 e join us! ***This concert is preceded*** by a short performance by talent
 ed students of The Royal Conservatory. **Prelude Recital starts at 7pm**.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31686
 6080/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261006T111704Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T111704Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/blackbird/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Blackbird: In the Footsteps of Ziryab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T200000
UID:blackbird-in-the-footsteps-of-ziryab-2026-11-20t20-00-00-05-00@agakhan
 museum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Oscar-de-los-Reyes-upper-body-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?re
 size=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Blackbird: In the Footsteps of Ziryab makes its world premiere
  as a bold new multidisciplinary performance celebrating the enduring conn
 ections between cultures through oral and artistic traditions. Led by Arti
 stic Director Amir Amiri\, the Amir Amiri Ensemble\, featuring Óscar de l
 os Reyes and Esperanza Soria\, the performance brings together Canadian an
 d Spanish Andalusian artists in a powerful artistic dialogue. Connected th
 rough centuries of migration\, poetry\, rhythm\, and memory\, the performa
 nce explores a shared cultural legacy while embracing new creative express
 ion. The essentials of flamenco are all present: voice\, complex rhythm\, 
 and dance.\n\nThis presentation ultimately asks how music travels through 
 history\, how cultures reshape one another\, and how artists continue to c
 arry ancient knowledge into contemporary life. The project seeks to illumi
 nate the enduring connections between Persian and Andalusian artistic worl
 ds\, while creating a contemporary performance grounded in research\, arti
 stic integrity\, and shared humanity.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/blackbird/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
