SUMMARY:Artists Circle: Anti-War Art with Pastels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T160000
UID:6ad76a7629c3d60033312972@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist\, our Artis
 ts Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress\, explore new 
 art techniques\, and connect with fellow art appreciators.\nThe theme for 
 November's Artists Circle is anti-war art. In recognition of Remembrance D
 ay\, this month's topic is inspired by veterans' various anti-war movement
 s including Veterans For Peace and the GI movement. Participants will lear
 n about anti-war art and veterans' anti-war movements\, and then they will
  be able to make their own anti-war piece using oil pastels. No experience
  is necessary and all materials will be provided!\nGuernica\n\, Pablo Pic
 asso\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad76a7629c3d60033312972
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
