SUMMARY:Sound and Sense: Jewish Music @York presents Pursue Peace
DTSTART:20261122T200000Z
DTEND:20261122T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260916T194000Z
UID:MEC-0e639bc3565415e8e31989d3cfc64161@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261122T200000Z
SEQUENCE:34
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/jewishnov.jpg
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,School of t
 he Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260916
DESCRIPTION:Contemporary Chamber Music by Canadian Jewish Composers\nAlbum
  Release Celebration Concert\nYork University’s Koschitzky Centre for Je
 wish Studies ( https://www.yorku.ca/cjs/ ) and the Department of Music ( h
 ttps://ampd.yorku.ca/department-of-music/ ) in the School of the Arts\, Me
 dia\, Performance and Design ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/ ) invite you to the 
 opening of the fifth season of Sound and Sense: Jewish Music at York\, wit
 h a special release concert celebrating Pursue Peace\, the initiative’s 
 debut album. The program brings together the work of three distinguished C
 anadian composers and leading performers in an evening of music shaped by 
 memory\, identity\, history\, and the many ways music gives voice to human
  experience.\nReleased by New Focus Recordings\, the New York-based indepe
 ndent label devoted to contemporary and creative music\, Pursue Peace feat
 ures composers Noam Lemish ( https://www.noamlemish.com/bio ) (ON)\, Sid R
 obinovitch ( https://www.sidrobinovitch.ca/ ) (AB)\, and James Rolfe ( htt
 ps://www.jamesrolfe.ca/bio/ ) (ON)\, whose music spans intimate works for 
 violin and piano\, string quartet and clarinet\, and a larger work for cho
 ir\, soprano and ensemble.\nMore than three years in the making\, the albu
 m is the culmination of an ongoing artistic collaboration at York\, bringi
 ng the work of Sound and Sense: Jewish Music at York to a wider audience. 
 We invite you to join the ongoing conversation through music and celebrate
  this milestone with us.\nSunday\, November 22\, 2026\nTribute Communities
  Recital Hall \n3:00 p.m.\nFREE \nRegister HERE ( https://www.eventbrite
 .ca/e/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music-by-canadian-jewish-composers
 -tickets-2001068522819 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260916
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ Accolade East Building 83 York
  Boulevard\, Toronto
ORGANIZER;CN="Israel and Golda Koschitzky Centre for Jewish Studies":MAILT
 O:cjs@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music
 -by-canadian-jewish-composers/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
