URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/25040/1795377600000
SUMMARY: Pursue Peace: Contemporary Chamber Music by Canadian Jewish Comp
 osers\, An Album Release Concert
DESCRIPTION:Album Release Celebration Concert\n\n\nYork University’s Kosc
 hitzky Centre for Jewish Studies and the Department of Music in the Schoo
 l of the Arts\, Media\, Performance and Design invite you to the opening 
 of the fifth season of Sound and Sense: Jewish Music at York\, with a spe
 cial release concert celebrating Pursue Peace\, the initiative’s debut al
 bum. The program brings together the work of three distinguished Canadian
  composers and leading performers in an evening of music shaped by memory
 \, identity\, history\, and the many ways music gives voice to human expe
 rience.\n\nReleased by New Focus Recordings\, the New York-based independ
 ent label devoted to contemporary and creative music\, Pursue Peace featu
 res composers Noam Lemish (ON)\, Sid Robinovitch (MB)\, and James Rolfe (
 ON)\, whose music spans intimate works for violin and piano\, string quar
 tet and clarinet\, and a larger work for choir\, soprano and ensemble.\n\
 nMore than three years in the making\, the album is the culmination of an
  ongoing artistic collaboration at York\, bringing the work of Sound and 
 Sense: Jewish Music at York to a wider audience. We invite you to join th
 e ongoing conversation through music and celebrate this milestone with us
 .\n\n\nFeaturing:\n\nAmy Hillis\, violin\, Katherine Dowling\, piano\, Sa
 ra Schabas\, soprano\, David Fallis\, conductor\, Maya Lahyani\, mezzo-so
 prano\, Noam Lemish\, piano\, Anthony Thompson\, clarinet\, Ilana Waniuk\
 , violin\, Carol Gimbel\, viola\, Mark Chambers\, cello\, Clark Schaufele
 \, chamber organ\, Nathan Petitpas\, percussion\, Jane Fingler\, soprano\
 , Vania Chan\, soprano\, Veronika Muggeridge\, alto\, Rebecca Claborn\, a
 lto\, Laura Chambers\, flute\, Cheryl Duval\, piano.\n\n\nProgram:\n\nAdi
 eu Babylon by Sid Robinovitch\n\nDi Mezinkeh by Sid Robinovitch\n\nPursue
  Peace by Noam Lemish\n\nSelections from Blood and Water by James Rolfe\n
 \nO Greenest Branch by James Rolfe\n\n\n“Sound and Sense: Jewish Music @ 
 York” is a performance and lecture series dedicated to showcasing the mul
 ticultural diversity of Jewish musical expression as well as the ongoing 
 intersections between Jewish and non-Jewish musical practices and communi
 ties. The initiative is driven by an inclusive philosophy that believes i
 n the power of music to serve as a bridge-builder and a vehicle for cultu
 ral exchange and dialogue.\n\n\nThe series has been made possible via the
  generous support of the Azrieli Foundation.
CATEGORIES:Concert
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6aed5bf1581a5a5025650619/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Album Release Celebration Concert York University’s 
 Koschitzky Centre for Jewish Studies and the Department of Music in the S
 chool of the Arts\, Media\,...
