SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T150000
UID:6ad7f450fee2d21deb24a82a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family.\nRuth Paul and Jonathon Vander
  Zee\, members of the\nOntario Bar Association\nwho practice Trusts and E
 states Law will speak about the elements of a will\, what happens if you d
 on’t have one\, what are powers of attorney\, why they are important and
  special considerations to keep in mind when preparing your estate and car
 e plans. Note\, this program is for general information only\, not for dra
 fting individual wills.\nPlease register for an email reminder and for us 
 to anticipate crowd size. Drop-ins welcome if space permits.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7f450fee2d21deb24a82a
