DTSTART:20261123T213000Z
DTEND:20261123T234500Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/25019/1795469400000
SUMMARY: The Stories We Keep: A Writing and Storytelling Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Bring an object that matters to you and spend an afternoon ex
 ploring its story through writing\, reflection\, and conversation.\n\nThe
  Stories We Keep is a guided writing and storytelling workshop about the 
 memories\, people\, places\, and moments held within the objects we keep.
 \n\nFor this workshop\, you’ll be invited to bring one meaningful object 
 from home and use it as a starting point for writing and reflection. Led 
 by a former archaeologist\, the workshop draws on archaeology-informed ap
 proaches to explore the stories\, memories\, and meaning we attach to the
  things we keep. Through a series of prompts\, exercises\, and conversati
 on\, we’ll explore the story behind your object and the memories connecte
 d to it.\n\nNo previous writing experience is needed. You don’t need to c
 onsider yourself a writer. Just bring an object that means something to y
 ou and an openness to see where its story takes you. Sharing your object’
 s story is encouraged\, but not mandatory for the experience.\n\nWhat to 
 Expect\n\n• A relaxed\, small-group writing workshop\n\n• Guided prompts 
 and writing exercises inspired by archaeology and personal storytelling\n
 \n• Workbook\, writing materials\, object description card\, and photogra
 ph will be provided.\n\n• Time to reflect\, write\, and share as much or 
 as little as you feel comfortable with\n\n• Conversation about memory\, o
 bjects\, and the stories we attach to the things we keep\n\n• A chance to
  leave with new writing about an object that matters to you\n\n\nWhat to 
 Bring\n\nOne meaningful object to write about. It can be anything: a piec
 e of jewellery\, an old photograph\, a childhood toy\, a handwritten note
 \, a souvenir\, a trinket\, a tool\, a book\, or something completely ord
 inary that holds a special memory.\n\nThe object does not need to be valu
 able or old. What matters is the story it carries for you.\n\n\nWho Is It
  For?\n\nThe Stories We Keep is for anyone interested in personal storyte
 lling\, memory\, objects\, and creative writing. Whether you already love
  to write or haven't picked up a pen in years\, the workshop is designed 
 to meet you where you are.\n\nCome curious\, come nostalgic\, come with a
 n object and a story you haven't quite put into words yet.
CATEGORIES:Workshop,Storytelling,History,Wychwood-Library
