SUMMARY: Like a Bird's Nest
DESCRIPTION:Sala-Manca Group (Lea Mauas and Diego Rotman) in collaboratio
 n with Meydad Eliyahu\, Brian Hoad\, Ktura Manor\, Itamar Mendes-Flohr\, 
 Yeshaiahu Rabinowitz\, and Nir Yahalom\n\nFENTSTER is pleased to present 
 a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective\, the S
 ala-Manca Group https://sala-manca.net/sala-manca-group . Installation\, 
 video and photography are exhibited together for the first time\, all con
 nected to the ritual object of the sukkah—a temporary hut traditionally e
 rected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot. Over the last twenty years\,
  Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and rel
 ated themes of shelter\, impermanence\, displacement\, and liberation.\n\
 nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies\, travelling through time
  and place\, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahal
 in Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar\; from the contested streets of Jer
 usalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario.\n\nExperience three full-siz
 e sukkah structures including a new outdoor commission from local artists
 : Maxine Lee Ewaschuk\, Rochelle Rubinstein\, and Jessica Thalmann. Thalm
 ann also debuts a window installation at the host venue\, PIX FILM Galler
 y\, that is on view 24/7.\n\nPresented by FENTSTER http://fentster.org/ i
 n collaboration with venue partner PIX FILM Gallery https://www.pixfilm.c
 a/\n\n\n\nExhibition Hours\n\nWednesdays & Thursdays 1 to 6 pm\n\nFridays
  to Sundays 1 to 5 pm
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Pix-Film-Gallery
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6ae028cc5309b65ff5082569/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Sala-Manca Group (Lea Mauas and Diego Rotman) in col
 laboration with Meydad Eliyahu\, Brian Hoad\, Ktura Manor\, Itamar Mendes
 -Flohr\, Yeshaiahu Rabinowitz\,...
LOCATION:Pix Film Gallery\,1411 Dufferin St Unit B\, Toronto\, ON M6H 4C7
 \, Canada
CREATED:20261027T043923Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055734Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T043937Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
