SUMMARY:Introduction to OnShape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T193000
UID:6ac665acebad22004543b279@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of 3D modeling working with free Onshape Comp
 uter Aided Design software.  This beginner class introduces essential Ons
 hape tools including: planes\, rectangles\, dimensions\, extrusion\, polyg
 ons\, spline\, sweep and fillet.  Students will work step-by-step to crea
 te a mug and gain skills to create their own design. No previous CAD exper
 ience required.\nBasic computer skills are required.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre\, 1st Fl
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac665acebad22004543b279
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
