UID:6ac823bb377296003a4aaf35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Cytron DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nEducational DIY Solar-Powere
 d Fan Kit\nSuitable for children aged 5 years and above\nProvides learning
  about renewable energy\nIncludes all components for easy assembly\nThe\nC
 ytron DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nprovides an engaging and interactive way 
 for children to learn about renewable energy sources. The fan\, which is p
 owered by a solar panel\, is simple enough to be assembled by a 5-year-old
  with the assistance of an adult. Children who are 5 years old and above c
 an independently assemble it.\nThe primary objective of this kit is to fac
 ilitate a better understanding of how solar panels and electric motors fun
 ction. The kit is comprehensive\, providing all the necessary components f
 or the assembly of the fan. These include wooden parts for the fan structu
 re\, a compact solar panel\, a small DC motor\, a propeller\, double-sided
  tape\, and cable ties.\nRegistration Begins  on October 26th 2026 at 10:0
 0 A.M. Spaces are limited this program will take place again in December.\
 nThe program will take place in the Auditorium located in the basement. El
 evator on site. If you have any questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 
 416-396-8910.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, The program will take place in the Auditorium located i
 n the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, please call 
 Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac823bb377296003a4aaf35
