SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Visualization Part 2: Tableau Public
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T153000
UID:6ad39ab5fee2d21deb23e549@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join this in-person program that introduces the Tableau Public
  platform to create and share data visualizations online. Participants wil
 l learn how to present data by creating simple charts and dashboards in Ta
 bleau Public. This workshop is for participants who want to develop basic 
 Data Visualization and Tableau skills.\nPre-requisites\n: Basic keyboardin
 g and mouse skills are required. Introduction to Data Visualization Part 1
  is recommended.\nA free Tableau Public account is required\n.
LOCATION:Humberwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad39ab5fee2d21deb23e549
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae8c2e8901b02002cc6d6ab"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Computer for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T153000
UID:6ae8c2e8901b02002cc6d6ab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on how to use a mouse for absolute beginners with litt
 le or no computer experience.\nIn this first session you will:\nObserve an
 d practice how to operate a mouse effectively\nUnderstand various mouse po
 inters and cursors\nReview basic keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for bas
 ic Windows functions\nUpon completion of this class students will be able 
 to use a computer mouse at a basic level and will be able to go online for
  additional practice.\nPrerequisites: No computer experience required.\nFo
 rmat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such
  as the mouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, ser
 vices and entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and
  friends\nInternet safety\, security and privacy\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae8c2e8901b02002cc6d6ab
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
