DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and      formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCr
 eate and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then      sort and 
 filter\nCreate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will 
 be able to get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPre
 requisites: Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and k
 eyboard skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformatio
 n Collection N\notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
