BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-on-thin-ice-are-lakes-feeling-the-heat/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub | On Thin Ice: Are lakes feeling the heat?
DTSTART:20261204T000000Z
DTEND:20261204T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T183700Z
UID:MEC-65d881fa9f6f1012fe15ae0402e93620@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261204T000000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/1
 0/YorkU-Alumni-Scholars-Hub.png
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261029
DESCRIPTION:We’re bringing Scholars‘ Hub to Vaughan for a special in
 –person edition at Bathurst Clark Resource Library. Bring your scientifi
 c curiosity and discover how climate change is reshaping freshwater ecosys
 tems in a thought-provoking discussion you won’t want to miss.\nAs globa
 l temperatures rise\, lakes around the world are losing ice cover at unpre
 cedented rates\, with far-reaching consequences for ecosystems\, water qua
 lity and public safety. At this special in–person edition of our Scholar
 s’ Hub series\, Professor Sharma will explore how changing winters are t
 ransforming freshwater systems\, and why mitigation of greenhouse gases is
  essential to preserving these ecological\, cultural\, and economically im
 portant resources. \nOn Thin Ice: Are lakes feeling the heat?\nDate: Thur
 sday\, Dec. 3 | 7 p.m. ET\nLocation: 900 Clark Ave W\, Vaughan\, ON L4J 8C
 1\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
ORGANIZER;CN="Alumni Engagement":MAILTO:alumnievents@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-on-thin-ice-are-lakes-feel
 ing-the-heat/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
