SUMMARY:Android Devices for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T153000
UID:6ad649a6de300e00451b6c93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for absolute beginners who are curious about buy
 ing an Android phone or tablet\, or who have just acquired one and want to
  understand how it operates.  Android phones include those manufactured by
  Samsung\, Google\, Motorola\, and OnePlus.\nIn this beginner’s class yo
 u will learn about:\n-the different parts of an Android phone or tablet an
 d where they are located\n-what you need to make your Android phone or tab
 let run\n-the Android home screen\n-settings\, storage and troubleshooting
 \nAt the end of the class you will have a basic understanding of how to ru
 n your Android device and where to find what you are looking for on your A
 ndroid device.\nBring your own device:  if you have an Android device\, fe
 el free to bring it with you and follow along with the exercises.\nPrerequ
 isites:  None\nFormat:  Lecture with hands-on exercises\n[90 min]\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649a6de300e00451b6c93
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
