DTSTAMP:20261107T055705Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T224500
SUMMARY:Free/PWYC Double Feature You've Got Mail + Winter Village (Distill
 ery District)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**Note: I recommend obtaining your ticket 
 as soon as possible\, as there are a limited number of seats**\n\n**On Tue
 sday\, December 8th\, see** **Soulpepper's Double Feature** **You've Got M
 ail and Shop Around the Corner\, plus get free\, skip-the-line entry into 
 the famous Winter Village at The Distillery District**. Be part of **Soulp
 epper's** **first dedicated Civic Programming lineup** rooted in a simple 
 belief: arts spaces should also be public spaces\, where people can experi
 ence culture\, exchange ideas and connect\, with or without a ticket. All 
 seats are general addminssion. **Purchase your Free/PWYC ticket for You've
  Got Mail and Shop Around the Corner on Tuesday\, December 8th at 7pm.**\n
 \n**Shop Around the Corner (1940):** Two employees at a gift shop can bare
 ly stand one another\, without realizing that they are falling in love thr
 ough the post as each other’s anonymous pen pal.\n\n**You’ve Got Mail 
 (1998):** A boutique bookshop owner and a corporate chain store owner who 
 despise each other in real life unwittingly fall in love over the Internet
 .\n\n**Costa Rica’s Río Celeste Chocolate Waterfall**\nSnack on chocola
 te-drizzled pineapple and banana treats\, then step through an augmented r
 eality portal to explore Costa Rica’s natural beauty.\n\n**Santa’s Vil
 lage at Soulpepper**\nInspired by Soulpepper Theatre’s production of “
 Parfumerie\,” this whimsical Christmas world takes over the theatre atri
 um. Step into Santa’s Village with twinkling lights\, displays\, a vinta
 ge-inspired letter-writing station\, specialty hot chocolates and\, of cou
 rse\, Santa and his elves.\n\n**Festive food and drinks**\nWith more than 
 50 vendors and outdoor bars\, the Distillery Winter Village is a true food
 ie destination. New this year: Prince St. Pizza\, Carousel Bakery\, Sweet 
 Crumble\, Potato Bar and Peacock Bakehouse. Chef’s Lane returns followin
 g a strong debut last year\, with four acclaimed chefs: Michael Angeloni\,
  Afrim Pristine\, Taylor Wells and Arush Vardhan Singh.\n\n**Naughty or Ni
 ce Bar at Pure Spirits Courtyard** — one of the village’s signature ou
 tdoor bars — now updated with 50\,000 white-and-blue holiday lights and 
 a long communal table.\n\n**COST**\nRegular: Pay What You Can $0/ 15/ 20\n
 Seats are general admission.\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy:
  All sales are final.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP\, confirming if you wi
 ll join for Winter Village only\, or Winter Village and the Movies**\n* **
 [Purchase](https://my.soulpepper.ca/16473/16483) your Free/ PWYC ticket fo
 r Tuesday December 8th at 7pm\, and post you have your ticket in the Comme
 nt section. I will then move you to attending.**\n* Members can also show 
 up at the Theatre at event start time with their ticket in hand.\n\nRSVPs 
 close 2 days prior\, hoping there will still be tickets. Cancellations may
  result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\nA reminder will be s
 ent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and whe
 n.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for the Winter Village at: 5:45pm in fron
 t of Young Centre for the Performing Arts in the Distillery District at 50
  Tankhouse Lane.**\nWe will wait 5 mins.\n\n**Meet me for the show at: 6:3
 0pm in the line for the Garland Cabaret inside the Young Centre for the Pe
 rforming Arts in the Distillery District at 50 Tankhouse Lane**\n\nOnce we
  have grabbed our seats\, we can take turns buying food inside the Theatre
  - sandwiches\, salads\, pastries\, beverages..\n\n**Show Starts**: **7pm*
 *\n\nYou've Got Mail Length: 2 hours\nShop around the Corner Length: 1 hou
 r 37 mins\n\n**After: meet at the same spot to chat about the show before 
 heading home**\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/316499446/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260910T144013Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T144013Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
