SUMMARY:The Real Dirt on Beauty Product
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T193000
UID:6aee1fadde685359098e711f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Many cosmetic ingredients have come under fire from environmen
 tal groups as being “dirty” and “toxic”. What should the consumer 
 believe? Louise Hidinger discusses the science of these ingredients\, alon
 g with a discussion of known environmental toxins and what can be done to 
 mitigate the risk of exposure.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welcome
  until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (1st Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aee1fadde685359098e711f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f48"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T193000
UID:6a6a661db57350d760b31f48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet online every Thursday evening\,\nSeptember 24 - De
 cember 10\, 6-7:30 PM\n(12 sessions).\nParticipants are expected to commit
  to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekly basis.\nLea
 rners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digital badge\ndown
 load a certificate of completion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aecd618ebad2200454aa1d4"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Graphic Novel Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T193000
UID:6aecd618ebad2200454aa1d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month to discuss a variety of graphic novels\, c
 omics\, and manga!\nFor November we will be reading and discussing\nSweat 
