X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T200000
UID:6ac6462e754bb0003ac33fae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us at Riverdale to share your love of literature! Ea
 ch session invites our members to read and discuss a new book each month i
 n a friendly\, welcoming setting. Ask staff for more information and help 
 registering.\nTom Lake\n\, Pickup Thursday September 10th\, Discuss on Th
 ursday\, October 8th\nEducated\n\, Pickup on Thursday October 8th\, Discu
 ss on Thursday\, November 12th\nClear\n\, Pickup on Thursday November 12t
 h\, Discuss on Thursday December 10th\nRemarkable Creatures\n\, Pickup on 
 Thursday December 10\, Discuss on Thursday January 14th
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac6462e754bb0003ac33fae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 10 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club 
 picks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libr
 ary. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Lib
 by\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
