DESCRIPTION:Explore mindfulness practices that support emotional well-bein
 g\, focus\, and self-awareness while experimenting with art-based exercise
 s that encourage reflection and stress reduction. No prior experience with
  mindfulness or art is required. Drop in. No registration required. This w
 orkshop is part of the Teen Social Health and Wellness programming. Genero
 usly supported by The Estate of Claudia Krawchuk.\nThis program is part of
  Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after schoo
 l and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nu
 tritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor
  call the branch to find out more.\nRegistration required\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada8dd2e9f71840dd72d345
