SUMMARY:2SLGBTQIA+ Expressive Arts Cookie Decorating Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T150000
UID:6ae230b029c3d60033331985@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Engage your creativity through the art of cookie decorating wi
 th Jasper Bryan\, an expressive arts therapist. This program is a welcomin
 g\, hands-on activity that introduces you to the arts and builds community
 . Participants will receive all the supplies needed to design their own un
 ique cookie while having fun connecting with others and expressing themsel
 ves.\nFood allergy notice: Please be aware that food will be used in this 
 program. Food products used in this program may contain or may have come i
 nto contact with common allergens. (*Contains dairy\, sugar\, and caffeine
 )\nThis program is for teens.\nRegistration\nis strongly encouraged but dr
 op-ins are welcome if there is space. Register online or call 416-393-772
 0.\nThis workshop is part of the Teen Social Health and Wellness programmi
 ng. Generously supported by The Estate of Claudia Krawchuk.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae230b029c3d60033331985
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa17f758cf597003f9241cb"}
