BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649a9fee2d21deb245197"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Android Apps for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261213T153000
UID:6ad649a9fee2d21deb245197@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for beginners who are curious about buying an An
 droid phone or tablet\, or who have acquired one and want to install apps.
  Android phones include those manufactured by Samsung\, Google\, Motorola\
 , and OnePlus.\n\nIn this beginner's class\, you will learn about:\n- what
  apps are\, and the benefits of using them\n- the differences between pre-
 installed\, free\, and paid apps\n- how to access and use the Google Play 
 Store\n- how to evaluate\, download and use apps\n\nAt the end of the clas
 s\, you will have a basic understanding of how to install apps on your And
 roid device through the Google Play Store.\n\nBring your own device: if yo
 u have an Android device\, feel free to bring it with you and follow along
  with the exercises.\n\nPrerequisites:  None\nFormat:  Lecture with hands-
 on exercises\n[90 min]\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649a9fee2d21deb245197
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae219968a335b6ae5ca9a2b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261213T153000
UID:6ae219968a335b6ae5ca9a2b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on basic keyboard functions for absolute beginners wit
 h little or no computer experience.\nIn this second session you will:\nFam
 iliarize yourself through practice with the most essential keyboard functi
 ons (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice proper keyboarding postu
 re\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use a keyboard 
 at a beginner level and know how to go online for additional practice.\nPr
 erequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 or basic mouse skills\nFormat: Hands
 -on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\\
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae219968a335b6ae5ca9a2b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
