DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T193000
UID:6ae5353b9dbc2b002c924526@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this hands-on class\, participants will measure an existing
  object\, model a replacement part in SolidCraft\, and prepare it for 3D p
 rinting using PrusaSlicer. Along the way\, we’ll discuss practical desig
 n considerations like strength\, material choice\, and iteration. Beginner
 s are welcome\, mouse and keyboard proficiency is strongly recommended. Re
 gistration recommended\, but we will try to accommodate all drop ins.\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
