SUMMARY:Apple Devices for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261220T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261220T153000
UID:6ad649ac29c3d6003330fc11@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for absolute beginners who are curious about buy
 ing an Apple iPhone or iPad\, or who have just acquired one and want to un
 derstand how it operates.\n\nIn this beginner’s class you will learn abo
 ut:\n-the different parts of an Apple iPhone or iPad and where they are lo
 cated\n-what you need to make your iPhone or iPad run\n-the Apple home scr
 een\n-settings\, storage and troubleshooting\n\nAt the end of the class yo
 u will have a basic understanding of how to run your Apple device and wher
 e to find what you are looking for on your Apple device.\n\nBring your own
  device:  if you have an Apple device\, feel free to bring it with you and
  follow along with the exercises.\n\nPrerequisites:  None\nFormat:  Lectur
 e with hands-on exercises\n[90 min]\n\nInformation Collection Notice: The 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649ac29c3d6003330fc11
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
