SUMMARY:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Mondays January 4 to March 1\, 2027\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nLearn the basics of throwing and trimming on the wheel\, explore hand building methods\, and finish your pieces with glazing. This 8-week class is designed for beginners. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional 10kg bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                     \n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 4\, 11\, 18\, 25\, February 1\, 8\, 22\, March 1\nNo class February 15 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Introduction to wheel throwing\nWeek 2: Trimming techniques and continue throwing\nWeek 3: Continue throwing and trimming\nWeek 4: Finishing trimming and introduction to glazing\nWeek 5: Introduction to hand building\, pinch pots\, and attaching handles\nWeek 6: Coiling\nWeek 7: Studio time\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Salina Ladha\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Salina Ladha is a visual artist and educator with over 15 years of experience in the arts. She holds a BFA with a major in ceramics and a minor in painting. Her work has been exhibited across Canada and she has been a guest lecturer at Concordia University\, presenting on hand-building and ceramic practices. She brings a thoughtful\, hands-on approach to both her practice and instruction. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-beginner-winter-2027/
