BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/stoneware-intermediate-winter-2027-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270224T163000
DTSTAMP:20261105T223424Z
CREATED:20261103T214845Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T223424Z
UID:148427-1799242200-1803486600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Stoneware (Intermediate)
DESCRIPTION:Stoneware (Intermediate)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Wednesdays January 6 to February 24\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nUsing stoneware clay\, refine your hand-building and wheel-throwing techniques\, and experiment with an underglaze relief printing technique and exciting glaze combinations on functional and sculptural pieces. You’ll also be introduced to press moulding and slip casting. This 8-week class is designed for students with previous experience who want to further their skills or reconnect with clay. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                     \n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 6\, 13\, 20\, 27\, February 3\, 10\, 17\, 24 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Hand building basic techniques\nWeek 2: Wheel throwing basic techniques\nWeek 3: Trimming and underglaze relief printing technique\nWeek 4: Glazing techniques\nWeek 5: Intro to slip casting and press moulding\nWeek 6: Slip casting and press moulding\nWeek 7: Completing and refining works\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Audrey Mah\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Audrey Mah is a contemporary ceramic artist living and working in Toronto. She studied visual arts with an interest in Sculpture/Ceramics at the University of Waterloo\, and graduated with a degree in Fine Arts. Audrey continued her ceramic arts education at the Ontario College of Art. While there\, she was awarded a scholarship which included a residency at the Instituto Allende in Mexico. Audrey’s work has been exhibited locally and internationally. She is inspired by the contrast in geometric and organic forms\, as well as ergonomic and practical forms of dishware. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/stoneware-intermediate-winter-2027-2/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-2.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-all-levels-winter-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270224T170000
DTSTAMP:20261105T223735Z
CREATED:20261103T214844Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T223735Z
UID:148486-1799244000-1803488400@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Wednesdays January 6 to February 24\, 2027\n2:00 pm – 5:00 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \nUsing stoneware clay\, learn to create functional and sculptural pieces on the pottery wheel. This 8-week class is designed for all levels. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                     \n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 6\, 13\, 20\, 27\, February 3\, 10\, 17\, 24 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nWeek 1: Introduction and throwing demo\nWeek 2: Trimming demo\nWeek 3: Throwing bowls\nWeek 4: Throwing cups and mugs\nWeek 5: Recreating the same form\nWeek 6: Throwing tall\nWeek 7: Studio time and underglaze demo\nWeek 8: Glazing\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh is a Toronto-based multidisciplinary artist whose work delves into the complexities of the human experience\, resistance\, and social change. Across various mediums\, including writing\, printmaking\, multimedia\, and sculpture\, Mohammad strives to convey deeply human and universal stories. His work has been recognized with several Canada Council for the Arts grants and an Access Copyright Foundation grant. Mohammad earned his BFA from OCAD University and was honoured as the recipient of the Sculpture and Installation Medal in 2020. In 2022\, he was accepted as an Artist-in-Residence for ceramics at Harbourfront Centre. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-all-levels-winter-2027/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-3.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
