X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/surface-decoration-combo-stoneware-all-levels-winter-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270107T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270225T163000
DTSTAMP:20261105T225043Z
CREATED:20261103T214728Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T225043Z
UID:148492-1799328600-1803573000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Surface Decoration Combo: Stoneware (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Surface Decoration Combo: Stoneware (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thursdays January 7 to February 25\, 2027\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \n\n\nCreate forms using hand building and wheel throwing\, then bring an illustrative quality to your ceramics using underglaze painting\, inlay (mishima)\, sgraffito\, stencils\, and more. This 8-week class is designed for all levels. Beginners are welcome\, but be ready to push yourself. \n\nThis class includes access to a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                     \n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 7\, 14\, 21\, 28\, February 4\, 11\, 18\, 25\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Make small pinch pots or plates\nWeek 2: Intro to underglaze\nWeek 3: Intro to inlay methods\nWeek 4: Intro to sgraffito and revealing inlay designs\nWeek 5: Intro to stencils and transfers\nWeek 6: Layering different techniques and studio time\nWeek 7: Trimming and finishing pieces\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Misbah Ahmed\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Misbah Ahmed is a Toronto-based multidisciplinary artist working primarily in painting\, ceramic sculpture\, and printmaking. Her art merges research on historical non-Western crafts and artifacts with a dedication to environmental themes\, reflecting her growing concern for ecological issues. Misbah completed a Bachelor of Design in Illustration from OCAD University in 2018\, where she received the program medal. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/surface-decoration-combo-stoneware-all-levels-winter-2027/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
