BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac43981c6cddb004595c4c9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Maintaining Cognitive Health and Managing Stress with Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T143000
UID:6ac43981c6cddb004595c4c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This seminar will discuss the latest research on the relations
 hip between stress\, lifestyle (such as exercise\, social engagement\, eat
 ing well\, managing stress\, and getting good quality sleep)\, and cogniti
 ve health to improve quality of life and facilitate healthy aging. Tips an
 d tricks for incorporating recommendations into the daily life will be dis
 cussed and there will be time for group discussion and a Q&A period with t
 he speaker\, Danielle D'Amico\, postdoctoral fellow at the Rotman Researc
 h Institute at the Baycrest Academy for Research and Education.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac43981c6cddb004595c4c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
