BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Walking\, Swimming\, Flying - Hands-On Nature
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T173000
UID:6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the different ways organisms move (and moved) around o
 n Planet Earth. Some walk\, some swim\, and others fly. Can you tell which
  is which? Participants will be able to handle\, study and learn about str
 ange objects: fossils\, replicas and modern specimens. They will be guides
  all through the how\, when and why these organisms adapted to move as the
 y do. Interactive\, entertaining and educational\, join us for a journey i
 n living locomotion.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hub
 s are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where h
 elpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered d
 aily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out 
 more.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae - Closed\, Youth Hub\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
