ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/
 11/chamber.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260925
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a dynamic midday escape featuring the Accolade Tri
 o\, York University’s premier faculty-in-residence ensemble. Clarinetist
  Patricia Wait ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/people/patricia-wait/ )\, cellist M
 ark Chambers ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/people/mark-chambers/ )\, and pianist
  Elizabeth Acker ( https://solidaridadtango.ca/elizabeth-acker ) take the 
 stage to breathe vibrant life into classical and contemporary masterpieces
 . Don’t miss this exceptional hour of brilliant chamber music\, performi
 ng live at the Tribute Communities Recital Hall.\nDate: Thursday\, January
  14\nLocation: Tribute Communities Recital Hall ( https://facilities.ampd.
 yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ )\nTime: 12:30 – 1
 :30 p.m.\nFree Admission\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall Accolade East Building\, York Un
 iversity @ 4700 Keele Street
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/common-hour-accolade-trio/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-assistant-certificate-in-teaching-tact-winter-2027-virtual-course/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Teaching Assistant Certificate in Teaching (TACT) – Winter 2027 
 Virtual Course
DTSTART:20270114T180000Z
DTEND:20270318T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260629T140100Z
UID:MEC-1677ff8f43415db89c2157e0f9e042aa@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270114T180000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/instructor-engagedsmallgroup-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Graduate Program in Political Science,Teaching &amp\; Learning
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260629
DESCRIPTION:Throughout this course\, you will have the opportunity to prac
 tice and experience different instructional strategies with peers from acr
 oss the university. Discussion and reflection will centre around the ways 
 in which your instructional strategies are informed by the teaching and le
 arning literature\, and the ways you use the strategies intentionally to a
 lign with your teaching beliefs and commitments to Decolonizing\, Equity\,
  Diversity\, Inclusion\, and Accessibility (DEDIA).\nBy the end of the cou
 rse\, you will\n– Connect and learn collaboratively with a community of 
 individuals committed to professional development in teaching and learning
 \n– Investigate the ways in which teaching strategies are used intention
 ally\n– Express and practice different teaching and learning strategies 
 to design and teach a 10-minute BOPPPS lesson giving and receiving feedbac
 k based on DEDIA and research evidence\nPlease note that registration clos
 es on January 4\, 2027 at 11:59pm ET.\nThe course will consist of five 2-h
 our synchronous sessions spread between January 14 to March 18\, 2027 (det
 ails below) via Zoom. Online learning and preparation between sessions wil
 l be required\, for a total time commitment of approximately 20 hours.\nRe
 gister using our registration form ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.y
 orku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1162122 ).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260804
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
ORGANIZER;CN="Teaching Commons":MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-assistant-certificate-in-teach
 ing-tact-winter-2027-virtual-course/
