BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f82"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 1: Create a Simple Spreadsheet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270201T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270201T150000
UID:6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f82@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for absolute beginner
 s with little or no Excel experience.\nIn this first session\, you will:\n
 Learn the basic function and design of Excel files\nPractice basic data en
 try for text\, numbers\, and basic functions: Sum\, AutoSum and Average\nC
 reate and save your first workbook and worksheets\nUpon completion of this
  class\, you will be able to use Excel at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: B
 asic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f82
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
